+# Reconnect using Voxy's existing terrain
+
+Date: 2026-10-05. Local follow-up to the user's observation that Voxy already
+owns a terrain cache. This supersedes unconditional source replay in the
+[earlier reconnect checkpoint](2026-10-05-dh-rejoin-cache.md).
+
+A cached DH tile is still decoded and validated locally. The client opens the
+current Voxy destination and reads copies of its level-zero sections on the DH
+worker. For each eligible Minecraft column, it compares every block state,
+quart-center biome and sky/block light value with the current DH conversion
+semantics. Water depth attenuation, negative coordinates, custom heights, air
+and default values remain consistent with the converter. A matching column
+gets a session-local content receipt without constructing Minecraft sections,
+converting Voxy mips or submitting an ingest. Missing or different columns are
+reconstructed individually from the retained source DTO. Section presence alone
+is insufficient. Voxy's ordinary `acquire` initializes absent sections, and
+the reader compares those actual defaults too. The pinned port initializes
+missing sections to fully skylit air; this cannot stand in for dark air or terrain.
+
+The server timestamp check still runs once after reconnect with continuous
+refresh Off. Unchanged replies carry no terrain payload. Offline changes fetch
+and deliver new source data. Full Voxy cache loss rebuilds from the source cache;
+source loss requires a timestamp-zero full request. Explicit reset clears both
+destinations as before. `/lss dhstatus` adds `Voxy reused columns`; conversion,
+enqueue and tile counters continue describing actual work rather than counting
+reads as imports.
+
+This is a bounded read/compare optimization, not a zero-IO reconnect. It does
+not persist a Voxy completion receipt. The reader holds the destination engine
+alive and releases every section after copying. Owned snapshots and mapping
+copies have budget reservations. Interrupted/timed-out client callbacks release
+a cache reader whose caller never received it, including completion/cancellation
+races. Optional read ABI failures fall back to the existing ingest path without
+disabling it. The installed port's classfile API was checked locally; other
+Voxy builds can use that fallback.
+
+The comparison covers level-zero content, not a new guarantee about every
+derived mip or future asynchronous write. A Voxy column refined by earlier
+vanilla visits may differ from the DH approximation and be conservatively
+rebuilt; the adapter has no persistent proof of that column's ownership.
+The [strict Voxy commit and vanilla-authority gap](2026-10-05-dh-voxy-commit-gap.md)
+therefore remains open. No upstream contact or Voxy production patch occurred.
+
+The normal Java 21 build passes 3279 unit tests (four existing Fabric skips),
+78 Fabric and eight NeoForge server gametests, all six LSS/VSS packaging checks,
+126 packaging selftests and nine SQLite helper tests. New pins check every
+compared voxel, water depth, quart-center biomes, negative coordinates, wrong
+blocks/biomes/lights, real Voxy defaults and owned-reader cleanup after timeout
+or interruption. No test-only observer is packaged in a production jar.
+
+The first warm run revealed unnecessary replay. Waiting for full target content
+in memory still reproduced it, ruling out the initial speculation that unfinished
